f(6n - 2005)\n   \\]\n   According to the functional equation:\n   \\[\n   f(f(n)) = 6n - 2005\n   \\]\n   Therefore:\n   \\[\n   f(6n - 2005) = 6n - 2005\n   \\]\n\n2. **Analyze the fixed point:**\n   We have:\n   \\[\n   f(6n - 2005) = 6n - 2005\n   \\]\n   This suggests that \\( 6n - 2005 \\) is a fixed point of the function \\( f \\).\n\n3. **Check the form of \\( f(x) \\):**\n   Since \\( f(f(x)) = 6x - 2005 \\), we hypothesize that \\( f(x) \\) might be a linear function. Let:\n   \\[\n   f(x) = ax + b\n   \\]\n   Substitute \\( f(x) = ax + b \\) into the functional equation:\n   \\[\n   f(f(x)) = f(ax + b) = a(ax + b) + b = a^2x + ab + b\n   \\]\n   According to the given equation:\n   \\[\n   a^2x + ab + b = 6x - 2005\n   \\]\n   By comparing coefficients, we get:\n   \\[\n   a^2 = 6 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad ab + b = -2005\n   \\]\n\n4. **Solve for \\( a \\) and \\( b \\):**\n   From \\( a^2 = 6 \\), we have:\n   \\[\n   a = \\sqrt{6} \\quad \\text{or} \\quad a = -\\sqrt{6}\n   \\]\n   Substitute \\( a = \\sqrt{6} \\) into \\( ab + b = -2005 \\):\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{6}b + b = -2005 \\implies b(\\sqrt{6} + 1) = -2005 \\implies b = \\frac{-2005}{\\sqrt{6} + 1}\n   \\]\n   Rationalize the denominator:\n   \\[\n   b = \\frac{-2005(\\sqrt{6} - 1)}{(\\sqrt{6} + 1)(\\sqrt{6} - 1)} = \\frac{-2005(\\sqrt{6} - 1)}{6 - 1} = \\frac{-2005(\\sqrt{6} - 1)}{5} = -401(\\sqrt{6} - 1)\n   \\]\n\n5. **Find \\( n \\) such that \\( f(n) = 6n - 2005 \\):**\n   Substitute \\( f(x) = \\sqrt{6}x - 401(\\sqrt{6} - 1) \\) into \\( f(n) = 6n - 2005 \\):\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{6}n - 401(\\sqrt{6} - 1) = 6n - 2005\n   \\]\n   Simplify and solve for \\( n \\):\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{6}n - 401\\sqrt{6} + 401 = 6n - 2005\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{6}n - 6n = 6n - 2005 + 401\\sqrt{6} - 401\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (\\sqrt{6} - 6)n = 6n - 2005 + 401\\sqrt{6} - 401\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (\\sqrt{6} - 6)n = 6n - 2406 + 401\\sqrt{6}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (\\sqrt{6} - 6 - 6)n = 401\\sqrt{6} - 2406\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (\\sqrt{6} - 12)n = 401\\sqrt{6} - 2406\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   n = \\frac{401\\sqrt{6} - 2406}{\\sqrt{6} - 12}\n   \\]\n   Rationalize the denominator:\n   \\[\n   n = \\frac{(401\\sqrt{6} - 2406)(\\sqrt{6} + 12)}{(\\sqrt{6} - 12)(\\sqrt{6} + 12)} = \\frac{401 \\cdot 6 + 401 \\cdot 12\\sqrt{6} - 2406\\sqrt{6} - 2406 \\cdot 12}{6 - 144}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   n = \\frac{2406 + 4812\\sqrt{6} - 2406\\sqrt{6} - 28872}{-138}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   n = \\frac{2406 - 2406\\sqrt{6} - 28872}{-138}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   n = \\frac{-26466 - 2406\\sqrt{6}}{-138}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   n = \\frac{26466 + 2406\\sqrt{6}}{138}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   n = \\frac{26466}{138} + \\frac{2406\\sqrt{6}}{138}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   n = 192 + 17.45\\sqrt{6}\n   \\]\n   Since \\( n \\) must be an integer, we check the integer part:\n   \\[\n   n = 192\n   \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( n \\) is \\(\\boxed{192}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{192}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"intermediate_algebra:569"}
